# An earlier session's inline reply comes back as it was (the fork's phase B): its text, how it
# answered (Reply All too: the store found only Reply's drafts before), and whom it went to when
# the user chose that: a recipient taken out of a Reply All doesn't come back after a restart,
# and the reply goes to whom its draft says. A draft to whom the compose rules plan (the same
# addresses, whatever their names) stays planned: Reply All then still adds the others. The
# drafts are in the store as a closed quick reply left them; the account's address isn't the
# samples' Alex Berg, so Reply All answers Alex too. The stand-in backend; every name, address
# and text is fictional. A reply that answers another way after its draft was first saved, with
# the store backend: reply-restore-kind.
# Run: tools/headless.sh 65 target/debug/pronto --self-test tests/selftest/reply-restore.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
layout-defaults app
resize 1440 900
# One row per message, as this script was written for: it follows single messages of a
# conversation (`conversation-show trip-6`). Conversation rows, the app's default since phase B,
# have their own scripts (conversations*.sealwax-test).
grouping messages
composer-backend stand-in
triage-mark-read-on-open false
conversation-account Personal ola.nordmann@example.test
# The Archive first: in Focused the list's cursor takes the Inbox's first row as soon as it
# arrives, and the reader lays its conversation out behind the list then, before the drafts below
# are in the store (an earlier session's drafts are there when Pronto starts).
folder archive
conversation-add trip
conversation-add links
quick-store-draft trip-6 "Ser dere fredag." reply-all tomas@example.test
quick-store-draft links-6 "Takk for lenkene." reply tomas@example.test
folder inbox Personal
list-wait
focus list

# Reply All with someone taken out: it comes back so, the choice kept.
conversation-show trip-6
key Return
wait-until assert-reader-on-screen true
wait-until assert-quick-reply text "Ser dere fredag."
assert-quick-reply kind reply-all
wait-until assert-quick-reply to tomas@example.test
assert-quick-reply cc none
assert-quick-reply chosen true
assert-quick-reply label "Reply to tomas@example.test"
# Sent, it goes to whom the box says.
action win.quick-reply
key <Control>Return
wait-until assert-quick-sends 1
assert-quick-send-last trip-6 "Ser dere fredag." reply-all tomas@example.test

# A reply to whom the rules plan: not a choice, so Reply All adds the others.
key Escape
wait-until assert-reader-on-screen false
conversation-show links-6
key Return
wait-until assert-reader-on-screen true
wait-until assert-quick-reply text "Takk for lenkene."
assert-quick-reply kind reply
wait-until assert-quick-reply to tomas@example.test
assert-quick-reply chosen false
key a
assert-quick-reply kind reply-all
assert-quick-reply chosen false
assert-quick-reply to tomas@example.test,alex.berg@example.test
assert-labelled
